(21061,181,'first_name','DAMAS'),
(21062,181,'last_name','KANYABWOYA'),
(21063,181,'description','Meet Damas Kanyabwoya a master of the written word, where precision meets poise. Based in the vibrant city of Dar es Salaam, Damas is not merely a journalist and sub-editor; he is a literary architect meticulously shaping narratives with depth, clarity, and purpose. With a career spanning over two decades in journalism, media consulting, and editorial leadership, he blends the soul of a storyteller with the discipline of a newsman.\r\nFrom the buzzing newsroom of Mwananchi Communications Limited to the investigative trenches of Tanzania’s most pressing social issues, Damas thrives at the intersection of facts and finesse. Whether it’s ghost-writing books, translating from Swahili to English and English to Swahili, French to Swahili and Swahili to French, editing thesis, transcribing in Swahili, English and French, producing meeting and workshop reports, copywriting for websites, social media platforms, managing people’s social media handles, or dissecting regulatory reforms, his work bears the unmistakable mark of intellectual rigour and narrative craftsmanship.\r\nEducated in philosophy, French, and mass communication — with academic footprints stretching from Tabora and Iringa to Burkina Faso and the Vatican-affiliated Urbaniana — Damas’s worldview is as expansive as his CV. \r\nA stickler for style and substance, he insists on meaningful context, and has little tolerance for journalistic clichés. When he’s not untangling complex policy texts or refining op-eds, you’ll find him jogging, travelling, or getting lost in the pages of a book — always searching for the next idea worth chasing.'),
(21064,181,'last_update','1750316852'),
